<title>USA: FINA buys stake in 7-Eleven chain.</title>
<headline>FINA buys stake in 7-Eleven chain.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>FINA Inc has acquired a one-third interest in a chain of 7-Eleven Stores for an investment of about $20 million, vice president Jeff Morris said Tuesday.</p>
<p>FINA, which is about 86 percent owned by Petrofina SA, said it formed a new convenience store company with Southwest Convenience Stores, which is owned by Don and Jack Wood of Odessa, Texas.</p>
<p>Morris said FINA contributed the cash and Southwest contributed its assets to form Southwest Convenience Stores LLC, a venture structured as a limited liability corporation.</p>
</text>
